{"type": "line", "artist": "Montana 700", "song": "Joy Road to Camp Wisdom", "line": "Free Big Meech, I pray they don’t catch me ’cause my brother hot (Woo)", "vault_lines": ["Free Big Meech, I pray they don't catch me 'cause my brother hot (Woo)"], "meaning": "Big Meech refers to a drug kingpin who was sentenced to prison time and will have his release date in January 2026. The brother lyric may also be a reference to the fact that Big Meech has a brother.", "annotation_id": "37130024", "url": "https://genius.com/37130024", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
{"type": "line", "artist": "Montana 700", "song": "Joy Road to Camp Wisdom", "line": "Ice J color, it hit different", "vault_lines": ["Street niggas, we built different, ice J color, it hit different"], "meaning": "When it comes to a diamond, there are two distinct scales that are utilized in order to determine the value of the stone: a clarity scale, which ranges from I3 to FL, and a color scale, which ranges from N-Z to D. J color diamonds are the last grouping of near-colorless diamonds that sit around the center of this scale, as they have a slight yellowish tinge that is noticeable under bright lights or magnification.\n\nFrom a value for cost perspective, J color diamonds are a great balance of both reasonable prices and beautiful clarity, making them ideal for the “iced out” jewelry many hip-hop artists wear.", "annotation_id": "34495580", "url": "https://genius.com/34495580", "state": "pending", "votes": 0, "second_sense": true, "clicked": false, "click_status": "api", "strength": "weak"}
